  if (Gt && ((0, import_chunk_cg8dqz0a.x)() === "linux" || (0, import_chunk_cg8dqz0a.x)() === "wsl")) oo.push(y ? "On Linux, each sandboxed command has its own private network: a server it starts binds without error, but no later command and not the user's browser can reach it, and a direct connection to a server outside the sandbox, on this machine or at a private address, fails too. The error is ECONNREFUSED, or ENETUNREACH for a private address (curl says \"Failed to connect\"), with no `<sandbox_violations>` block, so it says nothing about the server. To test a server, start it in the background, wait until it listens and check it, all in one command. If a server must stay up for the user's browser or later commands, retry the server as described above for a sandbox-caused failure, and tell the user in the same message that it runs without the sandbox's protection. A client that must connect directly to such an outside server needs the same." : `On Linux, each sandboxed command has its own private network: a server it starts binds without error, but no later command and not the user's browser can reach it, and a direct connection to a server outside the sandbox, on this machine or at a private address, fails too. The error is ECONNREFUSED, or ENETUNREACH for a private address (curl says "Failed to connect"), with no \`<sandbox_violations>\` block, so it says nothing about the server. To test a server, start it in the background, wait until it listens and check it, all in one command. If a server must stay up for the user's browser or later commands, tell the user it must run outside the sandbox, without its protection, as must any client that has to connect directly to such an outside server: they can ${In}; leaving the sandbox is their decision, not yours.`);
